You'll note that I pointed out that NetHack is *not* real life.  I'm
not saying that it should be (otherwise, you have a spelunking
expedition, no Amulet, no polymorph, etc., etc.).  What I *am* saying
is that, since we all have experience in real life, we have certain
expectations.  Among those is that a sword weighs more than a dagger;
Nethack includes that.  Also, having a rock fall on your head hurts;
Nethack does that, too.  Ice is slippery; again, this is in Nethack. 
Towels can be wrapped around your head, blocking your vision;
surprise--Nethack allows this as well.  Pets obey their owners, and
don't generally attack people without being provoked; oh, wait,
Nethack doesn't do that.  Why not?  So players--even lawful
characters--can rob stores and priests with impunity?  Does that make
sense?

To me, it doesn't.  If you think otherwise, by all means, tell me
why--that was part of my original post.  But don't arbitrarily discard
the idea because it's based on reality; most of the "cool" things in
NH are.

